   "pattern": {
    "name": "ni- for 'I', u- for 'you'",
    "explain": {
     "en": "The start of a Kiswahili verb shows who does it: ni- = I, u- = you. Ninatoka = I come from; Unatoka = you come from. The -na- in the middle shows the present. In speech, 'ninatoka' is often shortened to 'natoka'.",
     "fr": "Le début du verbe swahili indique qui agit : ni- = je, u- = tu. Ninatoka = je viens de ; Unatoka = tu viens de. Le -na- au milieu marque le présent. À l'oral, « ninatoka » devient souvent « natoka »."
    },
    "examples": [
     "Ninatoka Rwanda.",
     "Unatoka wapi?"
    ],
    "reviewed": false
